FEX: a 16 KiB interrupt fault page, so deferred signals are delivered (SteamARM, Darwin host)

FEX defers an asynchronous signal that arrives inside a signal-deferring
section, and makes the thread's InterruptFaultPage PROT_NONE so that the
store at the end of the section faults and delivers it. The page was
FEX_PAGE_SIZE (4 KiB) and 4 KiB-aligned. Under the runtime a host page is
16 KiB and carries the union of the protections of its 4 KiB pages
(runtime/subpage.c): the fault page's host page stayed read-write, the
store never faulted, and the deferred signal was never delivered. MEASURED
with x86-64 Android's mksh under FEX: a command substitution that runs a
program slept in rt_sigsuspend forever, 4 runs of 4, its child's SIGCHLD
deferred (trace: mprotect(0x...c03000, 0x1000, PROT_NONE), no SIGSEGV after
it); SIGTERM and SIGALRM did not end it either. The page is now 16 KiB and
16 KiB-aligned (the JIT's store offset stays within its immediate range; the
static_assert below checks it). SteamARM benchmarks/stage25-art-x86-fex.txt.

diff --git a/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h b/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h
--- a/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h
+++ b/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h
@@ -87,7 +87,17 @@
   uint8_t Size;
 };
 
-struct alignas(FEXCore::Utils::FEX_PAGE_SIZE) InternalThreadState : public FEXCore::Allocator::FEXAllocOperators {
+// The interrupt fault page below is a whole 16 KiB page, not FEX_PAGE_SIZE:
+// on a 16 KiB-page host (Darwin, under the SteamARM runtime) a 4 KiB
+// PROT_NONE page shares its host page with read-write neighbours, the host
+// page stays read-write and the store that should fault never does. A signal
+// deferred in a signal-deferring section then waited for a fault that never
+// came: mksh under FEX slept in rt_sigsuspend forever after its child's
+// SIGCHLD (MEASURED, SteamARM benchmarks/stage25-art-x86-fex.txt), and so did
+// anything else that got a signal while FEX deferred it.
+inline constexpr size_t INTERRUPT_FAULT_PAGE_SIZE = 0x4000;
+
+struct alignas(INTERRUPT_FAULT_PAGE_SIZE) InternalThreadState : public FEXCore::Allocator::FEXAllocOperators {
   FEXCore::Core::CpuStateFrame* const CurrentFrame = &BaseFrameState;
 
   FEXCore::Context::Context* const CTX;
@@ -128,7 +138,7 @@
   FEXCore::Core::CpuStateFrame BaseFrameState {};
 
   // Can be reprotected as RO to trigger an interrupt at generated code block entrypoints
-  alignas(FEXCore::Utils::FEX_PAGE_SIZE) uint8_t InterruptFaultPage[FEXCore::Utils::FEX_PAGE_SIZE];
+  alignas(INTERRUPT_FAULT_PAGE_SIZE) uint8_t InterruptFaultPage[INTERRUPT_FAULT_PAGE_SIZE];
 };
 static_assert(std::is_standard_layout_v<FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState>);
 // Maximum unsigned-offset store range for fault page.
